# AP Biology — flagship content. IDs prefixed 03- come from the master spreadsheet.
# Original definitions/questions pending teacher review. Not official College Board material.
@subject ap-biology | AP Biology | AP 生物 | Bio | green | 2
@desc From water's chemistry to ecosystems: the molecules, cells, genes and populations that make life work.
@framework Unit titles follow the public AP Biology course framework (8 units). Term placement is editorial and pending teacher review.

@unit 1 | Chemistry of Life | 生命的化学基础
@topic 1.1 | Water and Bonds | 水与化学键 | Explain how hydrogen bonding gives water its properties
- hydrogen bond | 氢键 | A weak attraction between a slightly positive hydrogen atom and a slightly negative atom such as oxygen or nitrogen | 一个分子中带部分正电的氢原子与另一个分子（或同一分子另一部分）中电负性强的原子（O、N）之间的弱吸引。单个氢键很弱，但大量氢键赋予水内聚力、高比热等性质，也稳定 DNA 双螺旋。 | Hydrogen bonds between water molecules explain cohesion, which helps water move up xylem. | 1 | #03-001
  mis: A hydrogen bond is a covalent bond inside a water molecule — it is an attraction BETWEEN molecules (or regions of a large molecule).
  rel: polarity; cohesion; specific heat
  vs: covalent bond
- polarity | 极性 | An uneven distribution of electrical charge across a molecule | 由于电负性差异，分子一端带部分负电、另一端带部分正电。水的极性使其成为良好的溶剂，并能形成氢键。 | Because water is polar, it dissolves ions and other polar molecules. | 1 | #03-002
  rel: hydrogen bond; hydrophilic
- cohesion | 内聚力 | The attraction between molecules of the same substance, such as water to water | 同种分子之间的吸引力。水分子之间的氢键产生内聚力和表面张力。 | Cohesion allows a continuous column of water to be pulled up through a plant's xylem. | 1
  rel: adhesion; hydrogen bond
  vs: adhesion
- adhesion | 黏附力 | The attraction between molecules of different substances, such as water and a glass tube | 不同物质分子之间的吸引力，例如水与植物导管壁之间。与内聚力共同造成毛细作用。 | Adhesion of water to xylem walls helps counter gravity during transport. | 1
  vs: cohesion
- specific heat | 比热容 | The amount of energy needed to raise the temperature of 1 gram of a substance by 1°C | 使 1 克物质升高 1°C 所需的能量。水的比热容高，能稳定生物体和环境温度。 | Water's high specific heat helps coastal climates and organisms resist rapid temperature change. | 2
  rel: hydrogen bond; homeostasis
@topic 1.2 | Macromolecules | 生物大分子 | Relate monomer structure to polymer function
- macromolecule | 生物大分子 | A large biological molecule built from smaller subunits: carbohydrates, lipids, proteins and nucleic acids | 由小分子单体连接而成的大分子，包括糖类、脂质、蛋白质和核酸。结构决定功能。 | The sequence of amino acids determines a protein macromolecule's three-dimensional shape. | 1 | #03-003
  rel: monomer; dehydration synthesis; hydrolysis
- dehydration synthesis | 脱水缩合 | A reaction that joins monomers by removing a water molecule | 单体之间脱去一分子水而形成共价键，从而构建聚合物。 | Amino acids are linked into a polypeptide through dehydration synthesis. | 2
  rel: hydrolysis; macromolecule
  vs: hydrolysis
- hydrolysis | 水解 | A reaction that breaks a polymer into monomers by adding water | 加入水分子使聚合物分解为单体，与脱水缩合相反。消化就是水解过程。 | Digestive enzymes hydrolyze starch into glucose. | 2
  vs: dehydration synthesis
- amino acid | 氨基酸 | The monomer of proteins, with an amino group, a carboxyl group and a variable R group | 蛋白质的单体。R 基团的性质（极性、非极性、带电）决定蛋白质如何折叠。 | A change in one amino acid's R group can alter how a protein folds. | 1
  rel: protein structure; macromolecule
- nucleotide | 核苷酸 | The monomer of nucleic acids, made of a sugar, a phosphate group and a nitrogenous base | 核酸（DNA、RNA）的单体，由五碳糖、磷酸基团和含氮碱基组成。 | DNA and RNA differ in their nucleotides' sugar and in the base thymine versus uracil. | 1
  rel: DNA replication; transcription
- protein structure | 蛋白质结构 | The four levels of protein organization: primary, secondary, tertiary and quaternary | 一级结构是氨基酸序列，二级是α螺旋/β折叠，三级是整体三维形状，四级是多条多肽链组合。 | Denaturation disrupts a protein's tertiary structure and can destroy its function. | 2
  rel: amino acid; enzyme

@unit 2 | Cell Structure and Function | 细胞结构与功能
@topic 2.1 | Organelles and Cell Size | 细胞器与细胞大小 | Explain how organelles cooperate; Relate surface area-to-volume ratio to cell size
- organelle | 细胞器 | A membrane-bound structure within a eukaryotic cell that performs a specific function | 真核细胞内执行特定功能的结构，如线粒体、内质网、高尔基体。分隔化使不同反应可以同时高效进行。 | The rough ER and Golgi apparatus work together to modify and package secreted proteins. | 1
  rel: compartmentalization; mitochondrion
- mitochondrion | 线粒体 | The organelle where most ATP is produced through cellular respiration | 有氧呼吸的主要场所。内膜折叠成嵴，增大表面积以容纳电子传递链。 | Muscle cells contain many mitochondria to meet high ATP demand. | 1
  rel: cellular respiration; ATP; endosymbiosis
  vs: chloroplast
- chloroplast | 叶绿体 | The organelle where photosynthesis occurs in plants and algae | 光合作用的场所。类囊体膜进行光反应，基质进行卡尔文循环。 | Light-dependent reactions occur in the thylakoid membranes of the chloroplast. | 1
  rel: photosynthesis; endosymbiosis
  vs: mitochondrion
- surface area-to-volume ratio | 表面积与体积比 | The relationship between a cell's surface area and its volume; it decreases as a cell grows | 细胞越大，表面积与体积之比越小，物质交换效率越低，这限制了细胞的大小。 | Small cells exchange materials efficiently because they have a high surface area-to-volume ratio. | 2
  mis: Bigger cells are always more efficient — larger cells have relatively less membrane for exchange.
  rel: diffusion
- endosymbiosis | 内共生 | The theory that mitochondria and chloroplasts originated as prokaryotes engulfed by an ancestral cell | 线粒体和叶绿体起源于被原始细胞吞入的原核生物。证据：双层膜、自身的环状 DNA 和核糖体。 | Mitochondria have their own circular DNA, which supports the endosymbiotic theory. | 2
  rel: mitochondrion; chloroplast
@topic 2.2 | Membranes and Transport | 细胞膜与物质运输 | Predict water movement using tonicity; Distinguish passive and active transport
- selective permeability | 选择透过性 | A membrane property that lets some substances cross more easily than others | 细胞膜允许某些物质（小的非极性分子）容易通过，而限制其他物质（离子、大分子）。 | Because of selective permeability, oxygen crosses the membrane freely while ions need channel proteins. | 1 | #03-006
  rel: phospholipid bilayer; diffusion
  vis: membrane diffusion
- phospholipid bilayer | 磷脂双分子层 | The two-layer structure of membranes with hydrophilic heads facing outward and hydrophobic tails inward | 细胞膜的基本结构：亲水的头部朝向两侧水环境，疏水的尾部朝内。这使膜对离子和极性分子形成屏障。 | Nonpolar molecules like CO2 pass through the hydrophobic core of the phospholipid bilayer. | 1
  rel: selective permeability; fluid mosaic model
- diffusion | 扩散 | The net movement of particles from higher to lower concentration | 分子从高浓度区域向低浓度区域的净移动，不需要消耗能量（被动运输）。 | Oxygen diffuses from the alveoli into the blood because its concentration is higher in the alveoli. | 1 | #03-007
  mis: Molecules stop moving at equilibrium — they keep moving, but there is no NET movement.
  rel: concentration gradient; facilitated diffusion; osmosis
  vs: osmosis; active transport
  vis: membrane diffusion
- osmosis | 渗透作用 | The diffusion of water across a selectively permeable membrane | 水分子通过选择透过性膜的扩散：水从溶质浓度低（水势高）的一侧流向溶质浓度高（水势低）的一侧。 | A plant cell placed in salt water loses water by osmosis and plasmolyzes. | 2 | #03-008
  mis: In osmosis, solutes move toward the side with less solute — in osmosis it is WATER that moves, toward the side with MORE solute.
  rel: tonicity; water potential; aquaporin
  vs: diffusion
  vis: membrane osmosis
  ipa: /ɒzˈməʊsɪs/
- tonicity | 张力（渗透压特性） | The ability of a surrounding solution to make a cell gain or lose water | 外界溶液使细胞吸水或失水的能力：低渗溶液中细胞吸水，高渗溶液中失水，等渗溶液中净水流为零。 | A red blood cell in a hypotonic solution gains water and may burst. | 2
  rel: osmosis; hypertonic; hypotonic
- water potential | 水势 | A measure of water's tendency to move, combining solute and pressure potential | 水分移动倾向的度量（Ψ = Ψs + Ψp），水总是从水势高处流向水势低处。加入溶质会降低水势。 | Water moves from soil into root cells because the soil has higher water potential. | 3
  rel: osmosis; tonicity
- facilitated diffusion | 协助扩散 | Passive movement of molecules across a membrane through channel or carrier proteins | 借助通道蛋白或载体蛋白顺浓度梯度运输，不消耗 ATP。 | Glucose enters many cells by facilitated diffusion through carrier proteins. | 2
  rel: diffusion; channel protein
  vs: active transport
- active transport | 主动运输 | Movement of substances against their concentration gradient using energy, usually ATP | 逆浓度梯度运输物质，需要消耗能量（通常是 ATP）和载体蛋白，例如钠钾泵。 | The sodium-potassium pump uses ATP to move Na+ out of the cell against its gradient. | 2 | #03-009
  mis: Any transport using a protein is active — facilitated diffusion uses proteins but no energy.
  rel: sodium-potassium pump; ATP
  vs: facilitated diffusion; diffusion
  vis: membrane active

@unit 3 | Cellular Energetics | 细胞能量学
@topic 3.1 | Enzymes | 酶 | Explain how enzymes lower activation energy; Predict effects of temperature, pH and inhibitors
- enzyme | 酶 | A biological catalyst, usually a protein, that speeds up reactions by lowering activation energy | 生物催化剂（多为蛋白质），通过降低活化能加快反应，本身不被消耗。活性位点的形状决定其特异性。 | An enzyme's active site binds a specific substrate, much like a key fits a lock. | 1 | #03-004
  mis: Enzymes are used up in reactions — they are unchanged and can be reused.
  mis: Enzymes add energy to reactions — they lower the activation energy barrier; they do not change ΔG.
  rel: activation energy; active site; denaturation
  vis: enzyme
- activation energy | 活化能 | The minimum energy required to start a chemical reaction | 反应开始所需克服的能量障碍。酶降低活化能，但不改变反应的总能量变化（ΔG）。 | Catalase lowers the activation energy for breaking down hydrogen peroxide. | 2 | #03-005
  rel: enzyme
  vis: enzyme energy
- active site | 活性位点 | The region of an enzyme where the substrate binds and the reaction occurs | 酶上与底物结合并催化反应的区域，其形状和化学性质决定酶的特异性。 | A competitive inhibitor binds to the active site and blocks the substrate. | 1
  rel: enzyme; competitive inhibition
- denaturation | 变性 | Loss of a protein's shape, and therefore function, due to heat, pH or chemicals | 高温、极端 pH 等破坏蛋白质的空间结构，使其失去功能（一级结构通常不变）。 | Above its optimal temperature, an enzyme denatures and the reaction rate drops sharply. | 2
  rel: protein structure; enzyme
- competitive inhibition | 竞争性抑制 | Inhibition in which a molecule resembling the substrate binds the active site | 抑制剂与底物结构相似，竞争活性位点。增加底物浓度可以克服竞争性抑制。 | Adding more substrate can overcome competitive inhibition. | 3
  rel: active site; noncompetitive inhibition
  vs: noncompetitive inhibition
- noncompetitive inhibition | 非竞争性抑制 | Inhibition in which a molecule binds elsewhere on the enzyme and changes its shape | 抑制剂结合在活性位点以外的位置（别构位点），改变酶的形状，增加底物无法完全恢复反应速率。 | Increasing substrate does not restore the maximum rate under noncompetitive inhibition. | 3
  vs: competitive inhibition
@topic 3.2 | Photosynthesis and Respiration | 光合作用与细胞呼吸 | Trace energy and matter through photosynthesis and respiration
- ATP | 三磷酸腺苷 | Adenosine triphosphate, the molecule cells use to transfer energy for work | 细胞的“能量货币”。水解末端磷酸基团释放能量，用于主动运输、肌肉收缩等。 | Cells couple ATP hydrolysis to endergonic reactions such as active transport. | 1 | #03-012
  rel: cellular respiration; active transport
- cellular respiration | 细胞呼吸 | The processes that break down organic molecules to produce ATP | 分解有机物（如葡萄糖）产生 ATP 的过程，包括糖酵解、克雷布斯循环和氧化磷酸化。有氧条件下以 O2 为最终电子受体。 | Cellular respiration releases CO2 as glucose is oxidized in the mitochondria. | 2 | #03-010
  mis: Plants do not perform cellular respiration — plants photosynthesize AND respire.
  rel: glycolysis; electron transport chain; ATP
  vs: photosynthesis
- photosynthesis | 光合作用 | The process that converts light energy into chemical energy stored in sugar | 利用光能将 CO2 和 H2O 合成糖并释放 O2。光反应产生 ATP 和 NADPH，卡尔文循环固定碳。 | In photosynthesis, the oxygen released comes from splitting water molecules. | 1 | #03-011
  mis: The oxygen released in photosynthesis comes from CO2 — it comes from water.
  rel: Calvin cycle; chloroplast
  vs: cellular respiration
- glycolysis | 糖酵解 | The breakdown of glucose into pyruvate in the cytoplasm, producing a small amount of ATP | 在细胞质基质中将葡萄糖分解为两分子丙酮酸，净生成 2 ATP 和 NADH，不需要氧气。 | Glycolysis occurs in nearly all organisms, suggesting it evolved early. | 2
  rel: cellular respiration; fermentation
- electron transport chain | 电子传递链 | A series of membrane proteins that pass electrons and pump protons to create a gradient used to make ATP | 位于线粒体内膜（或类囊体膜）上，传递电子并泵出 H+ 形成梯度，ATP 合酶利用该梯度合成 ATP（化学渗透）。 | A poison that blocks the electron transport chain stops most ATP production. | 3
  rel: chemiosmosis; ATP synthase
- Calvin cycle | 卡尔文循环 | The light-independent reactions that use ATP and NADPH to fix CO2 into sugar | 在叶绿体基质中进行，利用光反应提供的 ATP 和 NADPH 将 CO2 固定为糖。 | The Calvin cycle slows in the dark because the light reactions stop supplying ATP and NADPH. | 3
  rel: photosynthesis
- fermentation | 发酵 | An anaerobic pathway that regenerates NAD+ so glycolysis can continue | 无氧条件下再生 NAD+，使糖酵解得以继续，产生乳酸或乙醇。 | During intense exercise, muscle cells use lactic acid fermentation to regenerate NAD+. | 2
  rel: glycolysis

@unit 4 | Cell Communication and Cell Cycle | 细胞通讯与细胞周期
@topic 4.1 | Signaling and Feedback | 信号与反馈 | Describe the steps of signal transduction; Distinguish positive and negative feedback
- signal transduction | 信号转导 | The process by which a signal received at a receptor is converted into a cellular response | 信号分子与受体结合后，经过一系列分子（常有磷酸化级联放大）传递，最终引起细胞反应。三步：接收、转导、响应。 | A mutation that blocks a kinase in the pathway can prevent the cell from responding to a hormone. | 2 | #03-014
  rel: receptor; second messenger
- receptor | 受体 | A protein that binds a specific signaling molecule (ligand) | 与特定信号分子（配体）结合的蛋白质，可位于细胞膜上或细胞内。 | Steroid hormones bind intracellular receptors because they cross the membrane. | 1
  rel: signal transduction; ligand
- negative feedback | 负反馈 | A response that counteracts a change, returning a system toward its set point | 系统的输出抑制最初的变化，使其回到设定点，是维持稳态的主要机制。 | When blood glucose rises, insulin release lowers it — an example of negative feedback. | 2 | #03-013
  rel: homeostasis; positive feedback
  vs: positive feedback
  vis: feedback negative
- positive feedback | 正反馈 | A response that amplifies a change, moving the system further from its starting state | 输出进一步加强最初的变化，常用于需要快速完成的过程，如分娩、凝血。 | Oxytocin release during childbirth intensifies contractions — positive feedback. | 2
  vs: negative feedback
  vis: feedback positive
- homeostasis | 稳态 | The maintenance of relatively stable internal conditions | 生物体维持内部环境（体温、血糖、pH 等）相对稳定的状态，主要依靠负反馈。 | Sweating helps maintain homeostasis by cooling the body. | 1 | #03-024
  rel: negative feedback
@topic 4.2 | Cell Cycle | 细胞周期 | Describe the phases of mitosis; Explain how checkpoints regulate division
- cell cycle | 细胞周期 | The ordered series of events in which a cell grows, copies its DNA and divides | 包括间期（G1、S、G2）和分裂期（M）。S 期复制 DNA。 | DNA is replicated during the S phase of the cell cycle. | 1
  rel: mitosis; checkpoint
- mitosis | 有丝分裂 | Nuclear division that produces two genetically identical nuclei | 一次分裂产生两个遗传上相同的二倍体细胞，用于生长和修复。阶段：前期、中期、后期、末期。 | Mitosis allows a skin wound to heal by producing identical replacement cells. | 2 | #03-015
  rel: cell cycle; cytokinesis
  vs: meiosis
  vis: cell-division mitosis
- checkpoint | 检查点 | A control point in the cell cycle where signals determine whether the cycle continues | 细胞周期中的“关卡”（G1、G2、M），检查 DNA 损伤和染色体是否正确连接，由周期蛋白和 CDK 调控。 | A failure of cell cycle checkpoints can lead to uncontrolled division and cancer. | 3
  rel: cyclin; cancer
- apoptosis | 细胞凋亡 | Programmed cell death | 程序性细胞死亡，用于去除受损或多余的细胞，如胚胎发育中手指间组织的消失。 | Apoptosis removes the webbing between developing fingers. | 2
  rel: checkpoint

@unit 5 | Heredity | 遗传
@topic 5.1 | Meiosis and Variation | 减数分裂与变异 | Explain how meiosis generates genetic diversity
- meiosis | 减数分裂 | Cell division that halves the chromosome number and produces genetically different gametes | 两次连续分裂产生四个单倍体配子，且遗传上各不相同。交叉互换和独立分配增加遗传多样性。 | Meiosis produces haploid sperm and egg cells, each with one set of chromosomes. | 2 | #03-016
  mis: Meiosis produces identical cells — meiosis produces genetically unique haploid cells.
  rel: crossing over; independent assortment; gamete
  vs: mitosis
  vis: cell-division meiosis
- crossing over | 交叉互换 | The exchange of DNA segments between homologous chromosomes during prophase I | 减数第一次分裂前期，同源染色体的非姐妹染色单体交换片段，产生新的等位基因组合。 | Crossing over explains why linked genes are sometimes inherited separately. | 2 | #03-017
  rel: meiosis; homologous chromosomes; linked genes
- independent assortment | 自由组合 | The random orientation of homologous pairs at metaphase I, producing different allele combinations | 减数第一次分裂中期同源染色体对的随机排列，使不同染色体上的基因自由组合。 | With 23 chromosome pairs, independent assortment alone allows over 8 million gamete combinations. | 2
  rel: meiosis; Mendel's laws
- homologous chromosomes | 同源染色体 | A pair of chromosomes, one from each parent, carrying the same genes in the same order | 分别来自父母的一对染色体，携带相同位置的基因（等位基因可以不同）。 | Homologous chromosomes pair up and separate during meiosis I. | 1
  vs: sister chromatids
@topic 5.2 | Mendelian Genetics | 孟德尔遗传 | Use Punnett squares and probability; Distinguish genotype and phenotype
- allele | 等位基因 | A version of a gene | 同一基因的不同形式，如控制豌豆花色的紫色和白色等位基因。 | A heterozygous individual carries two different alleles for a gene. | 1
  rel: genotype; dominant
- genotype | 基因型 | The genetic makeup of an organism for a trait | 生物体某性状的等位基因组成，如 Aa。 | Two plants with the same phenotype can have different genotypes, AA and Aa. | 1
  vs: phenotype
- phenotype | 表现型 | The observable traits of an organism | 可观察到的性状，由基因型和环境共同决定。 | A purple-flowered pea plant has a purple phenotype regardless of whether it is AA or Aa. | 1
  vs: genotype
- dominant allele | 显性等位基因 | An allele whose trait is expressed in a heterozygote | 在杂合子中表现出来的等位基因。显性不代表更常见或更“好”。 | Because the purple allele is dominant, Aa plants have purple flowers. | 1
  mis: Dominant alleles are always the most common — dominance describes expression, not frequency.
  rel: recessive allele
- sex-linked trait | 伴性遗传性状 | A trait controlled by a gene on a sex chromosome, usually the X chromosome | 由性染色体（通常是 X 染色体）上的基因控制的性状，男性只有一条 X，因此更容易表现隐性 X 连锁性状。 | Red-green color blindness is more common in males because it is X-linked recessive. | 2
  rel: allele

@unit 6 | Gene Expression and Regulation | 基因表达与调控
@topic 6.1 | DNA to Protein | 从 DNA 到蛋白质 | Describe replication, transcription and translation
- DNA replication | DNA 复制 | The process of copying a DNA molecule before cell division | 以半保留方式复制 DNA：每条新 DNA 分子含一条旧链和一条新链。DNA 聚合酶只能沿 5'→3' 方向合成。 | Semiconservative replication means each daughter DNA keeps one parental strand. | 2
  rel: DNA polymerase; nucleotide
- transcription | 转录 | The synthesis of RNA using a DNA template | 在细胞核中，RNA 聚合酶以 DNA 一条链为模板合成 mRNA。真核生物 mRNA 还需加工（加帽、加尾、剪接）。 | During transcription, RNA polymerase reads the template strand to build mRNA. | 2 | #03-018
  rel: RNA polymerase; mRNA; translation
  vs: translation
  vis: central-dogma transcription
- translation | 翻译（蛋白质合成） | The synthesis of a polypeptide using the information in mRNA | 在核糖体上，按 mRNA 的密码子（三个碱基）顺序，由 tRNA 运来对应氨基酸，合成多肽链。 | During translation, tRNA anticodons pair with mRNA codons at the ribosome. | 2 | #03-019
  mis: Translation converts DNA into RNA — that is transcription; translation converts mRNA into protein.
  rel: codon; ribosome; tRNA
  vs: transcription
  vis: central-dogma translation
- codon | 密码子 | A sequence of three mRNA nucleotides that specifies an amino acid or stop signal | mRNA 上三个相邻碱基组成一个密码子，决定一个氨基酸或终止信号。遗传密码几乎在所有生物中通用。 | The codon AUG codes for methionine and signals the start of translation. | 2
  rel: translation
- mutation | 突变 | A change in the DNA sequence | DNA 序列的改变，可能是点突变、插入或缺失。移码突变通常影响更大。突变是新等位基因的最终来源。 | A frameshift mutation changes every codon after the insertion. | 2
  rel: natural selection; codon
@topic 6.2 | Gene Regulation | 基因调控 | Explain how operons and transcription factors control gene expression
- operon | 操纵子 | A cluster of bacterial genes controlled by a single promoter and operator | 原核生物中由同一启动子和操纵基因控制的一组基因，例如 lac 操纵子。 | When lactose is present, the lac operon's repressor is inactivated and the genes are transcribed. | 3
  rel: gene regulation; repressor
- transcription factor | 转录因子 | A protein that binds DNA to regulate transcription of a gene | 结合在 DNA 特定序列上、促进或抑制转录的蛋白质，使不同细胞表达不同基因。 | Different transcription factors cause liver cells and neurons to express different genes. | 3
  rel: gene regulation; cell differentiation
- gene expression | 基因表达 | The process by which information in a gene is used to make a functional product | 基因信息被用来合成功能产物（通常是蛋白质）的过程，可在转录、翻译等多个层次被调控。 | All body cells share the same DNA but differ in gene expression. | 2
  rel: transcription; translation; transcription factor

@unit 7 | Natural Selection | 自然选择
@topic 7.1 | Mechanisms of Evolution | 进化机制 | Explain natural selection; Compare selection, drift and gene flow
- natural selection | 自然选择 | The process in which individuals with heritable traits better suited to the environment survive and reproduce more | 具有更适应环境的可遗传性状的个体存活和繁殖得更多，使这些性状在种群中更常见。个体不进化，种群进化。 | Antibiotic use selects for resistant bacteria, which then become more common. | 2 | #03-020
  mis: Organisms develop traits because they need them — variation exists first; the environment selects among it.
  mis: Individuals evolve — populations evolve; individuals do not.
  rel: fitness; adaptation; variation
  vs: genetic drift
- fitness | 适合度 | An organism's relative ability to survive and produce fertile offspring | 生物体存活并产生可育后代的相对能力。进化意义上的“适合”看繁殖成功，而不是体力强弱。 | A smaller beetle with more offspring has higher fitness than a larger beetle with fewer. | 2
  mis: Fitness means strength or size — it means reproductive success.
  rel: natural selection
- genetic drift | 遗传漂变 | Random change in allele frequencies, strongest in small populations | 由偶然事件引起的等位基因频率随机变化，在小种群中影响最大。包括瓶颈效应和奠基者效应。 | After a storm randomly kills most of a small population, allele frequencies shift by genetic drift. | 2 | #03-021
  rel: bottleneck effect; founder effect
  vs: natural selection; gene flow
- gene flow | 基因流 | The transfer of alleles between populations through migration | 个体迁移或配子传播使等位基因在种群之间转移，通常使种群之间更相似。 | Pollen carried by wind between two meadows produces gene flow. | 2
  vs: genetic drift
- Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium | 哈迪-温伯格平衡 | A model in which allele frequencies stay constant when no evolutionary forces act | 在无突变、无迁移、无选择、随机交配、大种群时，等位基因频率保持不变：p² + 2pq + q² = 1。用作检测进化的“零假设”。 | If observed genotype frequencies differ from Hardy-Weinberg predictions, the population may be evolving. | 3
  rel: allele; natural selection
- speciation | 物种形成 | The formation of new species when populations become reproductively isolated | 种群之间产生生殖隔离从而形成新物种，可以是异域（地理隔离）或同域。 | A river that separates two populations can lead to allopatric speciation. | 2
  rel: reproductive isolation
@topic 7.2 | Evidence for Evolution | 进化证据 | Interpret phylogenetic trees and evidence of common ancestry
- homologous structures | 同源结构 | Structures in different species that share ancestry even if their functions differ | 来源于共同祖先、结构相似但功能可能不同的器官，如人的手臂与蝙蝠的翅膀。 | The forelimb bones of whales and humans are homologous structures. | 2
  vs: analogous structures
- analogous structures | 同功结构 | Structures with similar functions that evolved independently, not from common ancestry | 功能相似但起源不同的结构，由趋同进化形成，如鸟翅膀与昆虫翅膀。 | Bird wings and insect wings are analogous structures produced by convergent evolution. | 2
  vs: homologous structures
- phylogenetic tree | 系统发生树 | A diagram showing hypothesized evolutionary relationships among groups | 表示物种之间进化关系的树状图，分支点代表共同祖先。它是基于证据的假说。 | Species that share a more recent node on a phylogenetic tree are more closely related. | 2
  rel: common ancestor

@unit 8 | Ecology | 生态学
@topic 8.1 | Populations | 种群 | Interpret exponential and logistic growth curves
- carrying capacity | 环境容纳量 | The maximum population size an environment can sustain | 环境在长期内能够维持的最大种群数量（K），受食物、空间等限制因素影响。 | As a deer population approaches carrying capacity, its growth rate slows. | 2 | #03-022
  rel: logistic growth; limiting factor
  vis: logistic
- logistic growth | 逻辑斯谛增长 | Population growth that slows as the population approaches carrying capacity, forming an S-shaped curve | “S”形增长：开始近似指数增长，随着资源限制增长率下降，最终趋于 K。dN/dt = rN(K−N)/K。 | Yeast in a closed flask shows logistic growth as nutrients become limiting. | 2
  rel: carrying capacity; exponential growth
  vs: exponential growth
  vis: logistic
- exponential growth | 指数增长 | Population growth at a constant per-capita rate, forming a J-shaped curve | 资源不受限时种群以恒定比例增长，形成“J”形曲线：dN/dt = rN。 | Bacteria introduced into fresh medium initially show exponential growth. | 2
  vs: logistic growth
- density-dependent factor | 密度制约因素 | A limiting factor whose effect increases as population density increases | 影响随种群密度增加而增大的因素，如疾病、竞争、捕食。 | Disease spreads faster in crowded populations, a density-dependent factor. | 2
  vs: density-independent factor
- density-independent factor | 非密度制约因素 | A limiting factor whose effect does not depend on population density | 与种群密度无关的因素，如自然灾害、气候。 | A wildfire is a density-independent factor. | 2
  vs: density-dependent factor
@topic 8.2 | Communities and Ecosystems | 群落与生态系统 | Trace energy flow through trophic levels; Explain the effects of disruptions
- trophic level | 营养级 | An organism's feeding position in a food chain or web | 生物在食物链中的位置：生产者、初级消费者、次级消费者……每上升一级大约只传递 10% 的能量。 | Only about 10% of energy passes from one trophic level to the next. | 2 | #03-023
  rel: food web; energy pyramid
  vis: trophic
- keystone species | 关键种 | A species with an effect on its community much larger than its abundance suggests | 数量不多但对群落结构影响巨大的物种，移除后群落会发生显著变化。 | Removing sea otters, a keystone species, allowed urchins to destroy kelp forests. | 3
  rel: trophic level
- biodiversity | 生物多样性 | The variety of life in an area, including genetic, species and ecosystem diversity | 某区域内生命的多样性，包括遗传多样性、物种多样性和生态系统多样性。多样性高的生态系统通常更能抵抗干扰。 | Ecosystems with higher biodiversity tend to recover faster from disturbances. | 1
  rel: keystone species
- niche | 生态位 | The role and position a species has in its environment, including resources it uses | 物种在环境中的“职业”：利用的资源、生活条件及与其他物种的关系。两种物种无法长期占据完全相同的生态位。 | Two warbler species coexist by feeding in different parts of the same tree, partitioning their niche. | 2
  rel: competition

# ---------------- Practice items (original) ----------------
@q bio-u1-001 | UNDERSTAND | CONCEPT | SCENARIO | 1 | 1 | hydrogen bond; cohesion
? Water forms a continuous column that can be pulled up the xylem of a tall tree. Which property of water most directly explains this?
=* Cohesion produced by hydrogen bonds between water molecules :: Correct — water molecules stick to each other, so pulling at the top moves the whole column.
= Covalent bonds between water molecules :: Covalent bonds are within a molecule; between molecules there are hydrogen bonds.
= Water's low specific heat :: Water has a HIGH specific heat, and that property relates to temperature, not transport.
= Water's nonpolar structure :: Water is polar.
! Hydrogen bonds between neighboring water molecules give water cohesion; adhesion to xylem walls also helps.
!zh 水分子之间的氢键产生内聚力，使水柱连续；水与导管壁之间的黏附力也有帮助。
@q bio-u2-001 | APPLY | APPLICATION | SCENARIO | 2 | 2 | osmosis; tonicity
? A student places a plant cell in a solution with a much higher solute concentration than the cytoplasm. What will happen?
= Water will enter the cell, increasing turgor pressure. :: That happens in a hypotonic solution.
=* Water will leave the cell, and the membrane may pull away from the cell wall. :: Correct — the solution is hypertonic, so water moves out by osmosis (plasmolysis).
= Solutes will move into the cell by osmosis. :: Osmosis is the movement of water, not solutes.
= No movement will occur because the cell wall blocks water. :: The cell wall is permeable to water.
! In a hypertonic solution, water moves by osmosis from the cell (higher water potential) to the solution (lower water potential).
!zh 在高渗溶液中，水由水势高的细胞内流向水势低的外界溶液，细胞失水，发生质壁分离。
@q bio-u2-002 | UNDERSTAND | CONCEPT | MCQ | 2 | 2 | active transport; facilitated diffusion
? Which observation is the BEST evidence that a substance enters a cell by active transport rather than facilitated diffusion?
= The substance moves through a membrane protein. :: Both active transport and facilitated diffusion can use proteins.
=* Uptake continues even when the concentration inside is already higher than outside, and it stops when ATP production is blocked. :: Correct — movement against the gradient that depends on ATP is active transport.
= The substance is a small, nonpolar molecule. :: Small nonpolar molecules usually diffuse directly through the bilayer.
= Uptake is faster at higher outside concentrations. :: This is consistent with both mechanisms.
! The defining features of active transport are movement against the concentration gradient and dependence on energy.
!zh 主动运输的决定性特征：逆浓度梯度运输，并依赖能量（ATP）。
@q bio-u3-001 | APPLY | APPLICATION | GRAPH | 3 | 2 | enzyme; denaturation
? An enzyme's reaction rate increases from 20°C to 37°C and then drops sharply at 50°C. The most likely explanation for the drop is that
vis: enzyme
= the enzyme was used up by the reaction. :: Enzymes are not consumed.
= the activation energy increased at higher temperatures. :: Temperature does not raise the activation energy of the reaction.
=* the enzyme denatured, changing the shape of its active site. :: Correct — high temperature disrupts the enzyme's structure.
= the substrate concentration decreased to zero. :: Nothing in the scenario indicates that substrate ran out.
! Above the optimal temperature, the bonds holding the enzyme's 3D shape break. The active site no longer fits the substrate.
!zh 超过最适温度后，维持酶空间结构的键被破坏，活性位点形状改变，无法结合底物。
@q bio-u3-002 | UNDERSTAND | CONCEPT | SCENARIO | 3 | 2 | competitive inhibition
? A researcher adds an inhibitor to an enzyme reaction. When she greatly increases substrate concentration, the reaction rate returns almost to its maximum. The inhibitor is most likely
=* a competitive inhibitor. :: Correct — extra substrate outcompetes the inhibitor for the active site.
= a noncompetitive inhibitor. :: Noncompetitive inhibition cannot be overcome by adding substrate.
= a cofactor. :: Cofactors assist enzymes; they are not inhibitors.
= a denaturing agent. :: Denaturation would not be reversed by adding substrate.
! Competitive inhibitors compete with substrate for the active site, so raising substrate concentration overcomes them.
!zh 竞争性抑制剂与底物争夺活性位点，提高底物浓度可以克服抑制。
@q bio-u3-003 | MASTER | APPLICATION | WRITTEN | 3 | 3 | photosynthesis; cellular respiration
? Explain how photosynthesis and cellular respiration are connected in terms of matter and energy flow in an ecosystem.
r: States that photosynthesis converts light energy into chemical energy in sugar.
r: States that cellular respiration releases energy from sugar to make ATP.
r: Explains that the products of one process (O2 and glucose / CO2 and H2O) are reactants of the other.
r: Notes that matter cycles while energy flows and is eventually lost as heat.
! Strong answers connect both directions of matter (CO2, H2O, O2, glucose) and distinguish cycling matter from one-way energy flow.
!zh 好的答案要说明物质循环（CO2、H2O、O2、葡萄糖）与能量单向流动（最终以热散失）的区别。
@q bio-u4-001 | UNDERSTAND | CONCEPT | SCENARIO | 4 | 2 | negative feedback; positive feedback
? After a meal, blood glucose rises; the pancreas releases insulin, and blood glucose falls back toward normal. This is an example of
=* negative feedback, because the response counteracts the original change. :: Correct — the response reverses the rise in glucose.
= positive feedback, because insulin increases. :: Positive feedback would amplify the rise in glucose.
= signal amplification. :: Amplification happens inside signaling pathways, but the overall loop described is negative feedback.
= apoptosis. :: Apoptosis is programmed cell death.
! In negative feedback the response opposes the stimulus and restores the set point.
!zh 负反馈：反应与刺激方向相反，使系统回到设定点。
@q bio-u5-001 | APPLY | APPLICATION | MCQ | 5 | 2 | meiosis; crossing over; independent assortment
? Two siblings with the same parents have different combinations of alleles. Which processes during gamete formation BEST explain this?
= DNA replication and mitosis :: Mitosis produces genetically identical cells.
=* Crossing over and independent assortment during meiosis :: Correct — both shuffle alleles into new combinations.
= Transcription and translation :: These are gene expression, not inheritance.
= Binary fission :: Binary fission is asexual reproduction in prokaryotes.
! Meiosis shuffles alleles through crossing over (prophase I) and independent assortment (metaphase I); random fertilization adds more variation.
!zh 减数分裂中的交叉互换（前期 I）和自由组合（中期 I）重新组合等位基因；随机受精进一步增加变异。
@q bio-u6-001 | UNDERSTAND | CONCEPT | CLOZE | 6 | 1 | translation; transcription
? The process in which ribosomes read mRNA codons to build a polypeptide is called ______.
a: translation|protein synthesis
! Transcription makes RNA from DNA; translation makes protein from mRNA.
!zh 转录：DNA → RNA；翻译：mRNA → 蛋白质。
@q bio-u6-002 | APPLY | APPLICATION | PASSAGE | 6 | 3 | operon; gene expression
> In E. coli, the lac operon genes are transcribed when lactose is present and glucose is low. A mutant strain transcribes the lac genes even when lactose is absent.
? Which mutation would MOST likely cause this result?
=* A mutation that prevents the repressor protein from binding the operator :: Correct — without repressor binding, transcription is not blocked.
= A mutation that prevents RNA polymerase from binding the promoter :: This would prevent transcription entirely.
= A mutation in a tRNA gene :: tRNA affects translation generally, not lac regulation.
= A mutation that makes lactose bind the repressor more tightly :: Lactose is absent, so this would not matter.
! Normally, the repressor binds the operator when lactose is absent. If it cannot bind, the operon is always on (constitutive).
!zh 正常情况下无乳糖时阻遏蛋白结合操纵基因；若阻遏蛋白无法结合，操纵子将持续表达。
@q bio-u7-001 | UNDERSTAND | CONCEPT | SCENARIO | 7 | 2 | natural selection; genetic drift
? On a small island, a landslide randomly kills most of a beetle population, and the survivors happen to be mostly green. Green beetles were not better adapted. The change in allele frequency is BEST explained by
= natural selection. :: Natural selection requires survival differences caused by heritable traits.
=* genetic drift (a bottleneck). :: Correct — the survivors were determined by chance, not by their traits.
= gene flow. :: No beetles migrated.
= Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium. :: Allele frequencies changed, so the population is not in equilibrium.
! Random events that change allele frequencies are genetic drift. Natural selection is non-random: traits affect reproductive success.
!zh 随机事件引起的等位基因频率改变是遗传漂变；自然选择是非随机的，性状影响繁殖成功。
@q bio-u7-002 | MASTER | APPLICATION | MCQ | 7 | 3 | natural selection; fitness
? A population of bacteria is exposed to an antibiotic. A few resistant cells survive and reproduce. Which statement is most accurate?
= The antibiotic caused the bacteria to develop resistance mutations so they could survive. :: Mutations arise randomly; the antibiotic selects among existing variation.
=* Resistant variants already existed and had higher fitness in the presence of the antibiotic. :: Correct — selection acts on pre-existing heritable variation.
= Each individual bacterium evolved resistance during its lifetime. :: Populations evolve, not individuals.
= Resistance spread because of genetic drift. :: The change is non-random — resistance determines survival.
! Natural selection acts on existing variation; the environment does not create the mutations it selects.
!zh 自然选择作用于已有的变异；环境并不会“制造”它所选择的突变。
@q bio-u8-001 | APPLY | APPLICATION | GRAPH | 8 | 2 | logistic growth; carrying capacity
? A population graph shows rapid growth that levels off near 500 individuals. What does 500 represent?
vis: logistic
=* The carrying capacity of the environment :: Correct — logistic growth levels off at K.
= The maximum per-capita growth rate :: The growth rate is highest at intermediate population sizes.
= The population size at which exponential growth begins :: Exponential-like growth occurs early, at low population size.
= The number of individuals lost to density-independent factors :: The plateau reflects resource limits, not a fixed number of deaths.
! In logistic growth, the population approaches carrying capacity (K), where births and deaths balance.
!zh 逻辑斯谛增长中，种群趋近环境容纳量 K，此时出生率与死亡率平衡。
@q bio-u8-002 | APPLY | APPLICATION | MCQ | 8 | 2 | trophic level
? Producers in an ecosystem capture 10,000 kcal of energy. Approximately how much energy is available to secondary consumers?
= 1,000 kcal :: That is the energy available to primary consumers.
=* 100 kcal :: Correct — about 10% transfers at each step: 10,000 → 1,000 → 100.
= 10 kcal :: That would be tertiary consumers.
= 10,000 kcal :: Energy is lost as heat at each transfer.
! Roughly 10% of energy transfers between trophic levels; the rest is used for metabolism and lost as heat.
!zh 每个营养级之间大约只传递 10% 的能量，其余用于代谢并以热的形式散失。

# ---------------- Confusion Lab pairs ----------------
@pair osmosis-vs-diffusion | osmosis | diffusion
! Diffusion is the net movement of ANY particles down their concentration gradient; osmosis is specifically the diffusion of WATER across a selectively permeable membrane.
!zh 扩散：任何粒子顺浓度梯度的净移动；渗透：特指水分子通过选择透过性膜的扩散。
d: What moves :: Water only :: Any solute or gas
d: Membrane needed? :: Yes, selectively permeable :: No
d: Direction :: Toward higher solute concentration :: Toward lower concentration of that particle
s: A :: A red blood cell swells when placed in distilled water. :: Water moved across the membrane.
s: B :: Perfume spreads across a room. :: Particles spread down their gradient; no membrane.
s: B :: Oxygen moves from the alveoli into the blood. :: Gas diffusion down its gradient.
s: A :: Wilted celery becomes firm in fresh water. :: Water entered cells by osmosis.
vis: membrane osmosis
@pair mitosis-vs-meiosis | mitosis | meiosis
! Mitosis makes two identical diploid cells for growth and repair; meiosis makes four genetically unique haploid gametes.
!zh 有丝分裂产生两个相同的二倍体细胞（生长修复）；减数分裂产生四个遗传不同的单倍体配子。
d: Divisions :: One :: Two
d: Daughter cells :: 2, diploid, identical :: 4, haploid, genetically different
d: Purpose :: Growth, repair, asexual reproduction :: Sexual reproduction (gametes)
s: A :: A skin cell divides to heal a cut. :: Repair uses mitosis.
s: B :: Cells in the testes produce sperm. :: Gamete production uses meiosis.
s: B :: Homologous chromosomes exchange segments. :: Crossing over occurs in meiosis I.
s: A :: A plant grows new root tip cells. :: Growth uses mitosis.
@pair transcription-vs-translation | transcription | translation
! Transcription copies DNA into mRNA in the nucleus; translation reads mRNA to build a protein at the ribosome.
!zh 转录：在细胞核中以 DNA 为模板合成 mRNA；翻译：在核糖体上读取 mRNA 合成蛋白质。
d: Template :: DNA :: mRNA
d: Product :: RNA :: Polypeptide
d: Location (eukaryotes) :: Nucleus :: Cytoplasm / ribosome
s: A :: RNA polymerase moves along a gene. :: RNA polymerase performs transcription.
s: B :: tRNA anticodons pair with codons. :: Codon reading happens in translation.
s: B :: A ribosome links amino acids into a chain. :: Building a polypeptide is translation.
s: A :: A pre-mRNA is produced and later spliced. :: Pre-mRNA comes from transcription.
@pair selection-vs-drift | natural selection | genetic drift
! Natural selection is non-random: heritable traits affect reproductive success. Genetic drift is random change in allele frequencies, strongest in small populations.
!zh 自然选择非随机：性状影响繁殖成功；遗传漂变是随机的等位基因频率变化，在小种群中最明显。
d: Cause :: Trait-dependent differences in survival/reproduction :: Chance events
d: Leads to adaptation? :: Yes :: Not necessarily
d: Strongest in :: Any population with heritable variation :: Small populations
s: A :: Darker moths survive better on soot-covered trees. :: Survival depends on a trait.
s: B :: A flood randomly wipes out most of a small frog population. :: Survivors were chosen by chance.
s: B :: A few birds colonize an island and carry an unusual allele. :: Founder effect is a type of drift.
s: A :: Insects with pesticide resistance leave more offspring. :: Trait-based reproductive success.
